voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | clear, warm explainer","b":"gemini:Kore | bright, curious"}
prompt: "Why is the sky blue? #basic"

## Why is the sky blue?
level: basic

    path ground points [[40,90],[960,90]] hidden true
    ellipse eye_out x 180 y 122 rx 40 ry 22 hidden true
    shape eye_pupil #3d3833 shape circle x 180 y 122 radius 11 style.fill #3d3833 hidden true
    group eye members ["eye_out","eye_pupil"] hidden true
    label l_eye "You" left attach_to eye_out hidden true
    shape sun #d0865f shape circle x 860 y 640 radius 45 style.fill #f2c14e hidden true
    label l_sun "Sun" right attach_to sun hidden true
    polygon air dashed #8f887c points [[60,100],[740,100],[740,520],[60,520]] hidden true
    label l_air "Air" above attach_to air hidden true
    polygon sea #2f6b8f points [[770,110],[960,110],[960,250],[770,250]] style.fill #2f6b8f style.opacity 0.4 hidden true
    label l_sea "Sea" above attach_to sea hidden true
    mark sea_x around sea kind cross hidden true
    polygon glass points [[790,430],[900,430],[885,310],[805,310]] hidden true
    label l_glass "Clear air" above attach_to glass hidden true
    path beam #e0a93a points [[818,613],[600,480]] style.stroke_width 8 hidden true
    label l_beam "White sunlight" above attach_to beam hidden true
    path fan_red #b5482e points [[600,480],[408,425]] style.stroke_width 5 hidden true
    path fan_green #87a878 points [[600,480],[423,386]] style.stroke_width 5 hidden true
    path fan_blue #2f6b8f points [[600,480],[447,351]] style.stroke_width 5 hidden true
    path fan_violet #8a5fa8 points [[600,480],[477,322]] style.stroke_width 5 hidden true
    label l_red "Red" above attach_to fan_red hidden true
    label l_green "Green" left attach_to fan_green hidden true
    label l_blue "Blue" left attach_to fan_blue hidden true
    label l_violet "Violet" below-right attach_to fan_violet hidden true
    group fan members ["fan_red","fan_green","fan_blue","fan_violet"] hidden true
    shape card_box #8f887c shape rect x 865 y 430 width 235 height 250 shadow true style.fill #f4efe4 hidden true
    path card_blue_wave smooth #2f6b8f points [[770,524],[789,496],[808,524],[827,496],[846,524],[865,496],[884,524],[903,496],[922,524],[941,496],[960,524]] style.stroke_width 4 hidden true
    text card_t1 "Blue ≈ 450 nm" #2f6b8f x 865 y 466 font_size 22 hidden true
    path card_red_wave smooth #b5482e points [[770,424],[817,396],[865,424],[912,396],[960,424]] style.stroke_width 4 hidden true
    text card_t2 "Red ≈ 700 nm" #b5482e x 865 y 366 font_size 22 hidden true
    text card_t3 "Blue: 5–6× more" #2f6b8f x 865 y 325 font_size 24 hidden true
    group card members ["card_box","card_blue_wave","card_t1","card_red_wave","card_t2","card_t3"] hidden true
    shape m1 #3d3833 shape circle x 250 y 430 radius 7 style.fill #8f887c hidden true
    shape m2 #3d3833 shape circle x 560 y 260 radius 7 style.fill #8f887c hidden true
    shape m3 #3d3833 shape circle x 300 y 300 radius 7 style.fill #8f887c hidden true
    shape m4 #3d3833 shape circle x 650 y 400 radius 7 style.fill #8f887c hidden true
    shape m5 #3d3833 shape circle x 130 y 260 radius 7 style.fill #8f887c hidden true
    shape m6 #3d3833 shape circle x 520 y 170 radius 7 style.fill #8f887c hidden true
    shape m7 #3d3833 shape circle x 650 y 230 radius 7 style.fill #8f887c hidden true
    shape mol_b #3d3833 shape circle x 447 y 351 radius 10 style.fill #8f887c hidden true
    group molecules members ["m1","m2","m3","m4","m5","m6","m7","mol_b"] hidden true
    path red_cont #b5482e points [[408,425],[70,328]] style.stroke_width 5 hidden true
    arrow bounce_up #2f6b8f from.ref mol_b to.x 431 to.y 440 hidden true
    arrow bounce_right #2f6b8f from.ref mol_b to.x 532 to.y 382 hidden true
    arrow bounce_down mol_b -> dusk_glow #2f6b8f hidden true
    arrow bounce_eye mol_b -> eye #2f6b8f hidden true
    group bounce members ["bounce_up","bounce_right","bounce_down","bounce_eye"] hidden true
    arrow a1 m1 -> eye #2f6b8f hidden true
    arrow a2 m2 -> eye #2f6b8f hidden true
    arrow a3 m3 -> eye #2f6b8f hidden true
    arrow a5 m5 -> eye #2f6b8f hidden true
    polygon sky_tint #2f6b8f points [[60,100],[740,100],[740,520],[60,520]] style.fill #2f6b8f style.opacity 0.2 hidden true
    group noon members ["beam","fan","red_cont","bounce","a1","a2","a3","a5","sky_tint"] hidden true
    path dusk_beam #e0a93a points [[835,210],[228,125]] style.stroke_width 7 hidden true
    label l_dusk "Long road" below attach_to dusk_beam hidden true
    label l_noon "Short road" below-left attach_to beam hidden true
    arrow bo1 #2f6b8f from.x 700 from.y 191 to.x 712 to.y 270 hidden true
    arrow bo2 #2f6b8f from.x 610 from.y 179 to.x 598 to.y 118 hidden true
    arrow bo3 #2f6b8f from.ref m6 to.x 535 to.y 245 hidden true
    arrow bo4 #2f6b8f from.x 420 from.y 152 to.x 410 to.y 222 hidden true
    group blue_out members ["bo1","bo2","bo3","bo4"] hidden true
    path dusk_red #b5482e points [[640,183],[228,125]] style.stroke_width 7 hidden true
    polygon dusk_glow #b5482e points [[470,100],[740,100],[740,320],[470,320]] style.fill #b5482e style.opacity 0.22 hidden true
    group dusk members ["dusk_beam","dusk_red","dusk_glow","blue_out"] hidden true
    text claim "Blue scatters most." #2f6b8f x 330 y 640 font_size 34 hidden true
    mark claim_box around claim kind box hidden true
    figure fig aspect 4:3 box full members ["ground","eye_out","eye_pupil","l_eye","sun","l_sun","air","l_air","sea","l_sea","sea_x","glass","l_glass","beam","l_beam","fan_red","fan_green","fan_blue","fan_violet","l_red","l_green","l_blue","l_violet","card_box","card_blue_wave","card_t1","card_red_wave","card_t2","card_t3","m1","m2","m3","m4","m5","m6","m7","mol_b","red_cont","bounce_up","bounce_right","bounce_down","bounce_eye","a1","a2","a3","a5","sky_tint","dusk_beam","l_dusk","l_noon","bo1","bo2","bo3","bo4","dusk_red","dusk_glow","claim","claim_box"] hidden true

    card title "Why is the sky blue?"

Why is the sky blue?
    draw ground eye l_eye sun l_sun air l_air

Many people guess the sky is blue because it mirrors the sea, or because air is simply blue.
    draw sea l_sea sea_x

But air in a glass is clear, and the sea is actually blue for a different reason.
    draw glass l_glass

    pause 0.5

    erase glass l_glass sea l_sea sea_x parallel true

So the answer must be in the sunlight itself.
    draw beam l_beam

Sunlight looks white, but it is a mix of every color, just like the rainbow you see after rain.
    draw fan_red l_red fan_green l_green fan_blue l_blue fan_violet l_violet

Each color travels as a wave, and blue waves are shorter than red waves.
    draw card_box card_blue_wave card_t1 card_red_wave card_t2

The air is full of tiny molecules, far smaller than those waves, and they act like little pins in a pinball machine.
    draw molecules parallel true

Long red waves slip past them almost untouched,
    draw red_cont

but short blue waves get knocked about in all directions.
    draw bounce_up bounce_right bounce_down bounce_eye card_t3

Blue is bounced around so much that it ends up coming from everywhere, so when you look at any patch of sky, some of that blue lands in your eye.
    draw a1 a2 a3 a5 parallel true

    draw sky_tint

You may ask why the sky is not violet, since violet is even shorter.
    highlight fan_violet l_violet effect circle

The sun gives out less violet, the upper air soaks up some, and our eyes are less sensitive to it,
    fade fan_violet to 0.15

so blue wins.
    highlight fan_blue l_blue

    erase card_box card_blue_wave card_t1 card_red_wave card_t2 card_t3 parallel true

Now imagine the sun sinking toward the horizon,
    fade noon to 0.2

so its light has a much longer road through the air.
    move sun by [20,-425] duration 3 ghost true

    draw dusk_beam

Its light now crosses so much air that most of the blue is bounced away before reaching you,
    draw bo1 bo2 bo3 bo4 parallel true

and the reds and oranges are what remain.
    draw dusk_red dusk_glow

    fade dusk to 0.25 duration 0.8

    fade noon sun_ghost to 1 duration 0.8

So the sky is blue because air scatters the short blue waves of sunlight in every direction.
    draw claim claim_box

And a sunset is the same story, only with a longer road for the light.
    fade dusk to 1

    draw l_noon l_dusk parallel true

    quiz "On a planet whose air scatters light the same way, a sunbeam holds only red and violet. Which color is scattered more, and so is more likely to fill that planet's sky?"
        intro: Your turn: which color would be scattered most?
        right: Violet: the shorter the wave, the more the tiny molecules knock it about, so it fills that planet's sky.
        wrong: Think about which waves the tiny molecules knock about more easily: the long ones that slip past, or the short ones.
        * Red, the longest wave
        + Violet, the shorter wave
        * Both the same, air is clear

So the sky was never blue paint, only sunlight sorted by the air.
    fade noon dusk sun sun_ghost air ground eye claim claim_box molecules to 0.12 duration 2

